                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "60bc13bb-c950-41e1-81ef-85a651400e7b",
                        "source_entry_id": "b6a55c45-8e3d-3644-a628-bdd27a8ad2fb",
                        "source_sense_id": "b1b73097-4db2-324f-82e1-78b00dbab5cc",
                        "target_lang_word": "railman",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "railman",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d34fbeb3-16fd-369e-86b6-b53b9f9fae9a",
                                        "entry_id": "5b844d8c-2af3-3fff-aef1-66287f881b75",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A man who works on a railway."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9e744452-61d8-47b7-b42d-d06f3cdb21c9",
                                                "sense_id": "d34fbeb3-16fd-369e-86b6-b53b9f9fae9a",
                                                "text": "\"The railman on the platform, whom I knew well, looked a bit bemused and asked what I was doing. Thinking it a silly question, I said something along the lines of 'what do you think? I'm going home to bed'.\n\"He then said 'but you don't live here anymore'."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "983182b1-9432-4fa6-9a88-c1f164c85269",
                                                "sense_id": "d34fbeb3-16fd-369e-86b6-b53b9f9fae9a",
                                                "text": "There was also a belief that they had been taken advantage of - \"kicked from pillar to post, the bottom dogs in the labour market because of the inherent love of railmen for their jobs\", according to one NUR member."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "66f8bcea-5031-471f-99a5-700397170f30",
                        "source_entry_id": "b6a55c45-8e3d-3644-a628-bdd27a8ad2fb",
                        "source_sense_id": "b1b73097-4db2-324f-82e1-78b00dbab5cc",
                        "target_lang_word": "railwayman",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "railwayman",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "76aff20e-2b8b-3950-b6d0-dd91512d0315",
                                        "entry_id": "4dfa9676-64de-37ad-9c7e-97b36f007002",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A man who works on a railway."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d961d9b5-9a80-44e6-a7c3-782cd78c165b",
                                                "sense_id": "76aff20e-2b8b-3950-b6d0-dd91512d0315",
                                                "text": "The spirit of the local railwaymen in this emergency is shown by the Helensburgh fireman who heard the news at 8 a.m. on his radio and immediately went to the depot of his own accord to see what help he could give."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9939b6e7-3846-4f98-b5f1-928556fe75f0",
                                                "sense_id": "76aff20e-2b8b-3950-b6d0-dd91512d0315",
                                                "text": "Nizan was, of course, Marxist and he did use his Marxist intelligence—although, thank God, never the jargon—to show the [economic] and emotional cost of the life of Antoine Bloye, a [working‐class] railwayman who made the painful rise to become a railway functionary and a member of the petit bourgeoisie."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b60ef028-d15e-4814-bf26-6e69d8262f9e",
                        "source_entry_id": "b6a55c45-8e3d-3644-a628-bdd27a8ad2fb",
                        "source_sense_id": "b1b73097-4db2-324f-82e1-78b00dbab5cc",
